---
import './keys.css';
---
<figure class="key-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 4</span>Two different meanings of version</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="pair"><div class="box"><div class="label">The product changes</div><strong>GBP 20.00 → GBP 22.00</strong><span><code>revision: 1 → 2</code></span><span>The v1 format still uses integer price_pence.</span></div><div class="box"><div class="label">The representation changes</div><strong>Pence → a formatted price string</strong><span><code>v1 → v2</code>, if incompatible</span><span>The same source revision can be encoded in either format.</span></div></div>
  <div class="pair"><div class="box"><strong>Old reader</strong><span>Expects <code>price_pence: 2000</code></span><span>Divides by 100 to display pounds.</span></div><div class="box"><strong>Hypothetical new reader</strong><span>Expects <code>display_price: "£20.00"</code></span><span>Displays an already formatted string.</span></div></div>
  <p class="result">A readable JSON object is not enough. Each reader must understand the field’s name, type and meaning.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>The v2 card is an illustrative format change, not a change to the worked v1 adapter. Changing the source price does not require renaming the format namespace.</figcaption>
</figure>
